Package: OncoCohortSelect
Type: Package
Title: Cohort Selection by Posterior Benefit-Risk and Win Statistics
Version: 0.3.3
Authors@R: person(given = "Gosuke",
                  family = "Homma",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com")
Description: Selects one of several single-arm oncology cohorts with multiple
    efficacy and safety endpoints for further development, and evaluates the
    selection rules by simulation. A posterior benefit-risk score combines the
    posterior probabilities that response rates, survival probabilities or
    hazard ratios are favorable, against target values or relative to a
    reference cohort, following Chakraborty et al. (2026)
    <doi:10.1080/19466315.2026.2668381>. Generalized pairwise comparisons of
    prioritized binary and time-to-event endpoints (Buyse (2010)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.3923>), with the scoring rule of Gehan or of Peron et al.
    (2018) <doi:10.1177/0962280216658320> for censored times, give the net
    treatment benefit, the win ratio and the win odds with standard errors.
    Correlated progression-free survival, overall survival and objective
    response are simulated with the 'CorOncoEndpoints' package, an independent
    adverse event is added, and decision rules that select one of two or more
    cohorts are compared at a common probability of a false selection.
